Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:58:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Knowledge: the seventh judgement round's defects

Only a name with nothing at it is gone. A link or a file put where a repository's folder was is refused by name: rebuild, list and adopt set it aside and keep its rows, and a write makes no second folder beside it. The name a project's row holds is the project's while anything is at it, so a folder whose manifest is gone or unreadable, or that cannot be looked into, is never traded for a new one. An entries or proposals folder that cannot be listed, or a name in it that cannot be looked at, refuses the rebuild instead of replacing the rows with none. doctor lists the folders with the module's own lookAt, kindAt and namesIn, and gives the same answer with and without a database.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
